# Chroma library, modern Earth: the gathering sphere's events as they touch a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3). Design: chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-data/gather.json (events with on_character and the modern epoch; each scene is built on the
# event's wording.modern and on_character). Face words: chroma-library/earth_spheres.py. Fields: build.py (the spheres'
# fields of world-fields.md, 2026-10-09).
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event the Engine fires on its sphere event (sphere_event: <key>) for the
# people its selector names (place, members or all); per_year is all 0 and there are no drivers. The '# world:' line
# above each moment gives the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who meet the moment (estimate).
# Seventeen moments, one per gather event of the modern epoch that has on_character, except great_feast (another writer
# has the great gathering). Tone follows the event's tone (good = joy, bad = trouble, mixed = mixed): 6 joy, 6 trouble,
# 5 mixed.
#
# Options: sphere: on each is the face the act is in (one-colour X: gather.X; a pair: its pair face in wheel order, so
# WR is gather.RW, WG gather.GW, UG gather.GU). Levers (lever:) where the act plainly is one, from character.levers.
# The brawl moment is the morning after (the witness statement, the hospital, the other side's story), since 'a pub
# argument turns into a fight' (earth-crime.lib) already holds the fight itself.
#
# Layout: each a life event with the five one-colour options and one pair set. The 17 use all twelve halves of D1 to D6,
# five of them twice (D1b, D2b, D3a, D5b, D6a), each chosen to hold the event's own pair faces where it has them.
# Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so every
# colour has the same mean chance in each moment and in every stage. No flags.
#
# share: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3a) is its '# world:' share: the engine draws at birth who can
# ever meet it, so when the event comes to town only that share of the people there are open to the moment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- meeting_place_opens (pairs D2a)

# world: sphere event meeting_place_opens, selector place, share .3
== a new café on the corner
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: meeting_place_opens
share: .3
haunt: gather.house
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 15-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 4-15
times: World event: meeting_place_opens (sphere gather). Selector place: a new meeting place opens in a growing quarter or a town with free time and wages rising; about 3 in 10 of the people living near it try it and feel the pull between the new place and the old (share .3, estimate), a few times in a life (estimate)
likelier: a growing quarter, rising wages and free evenings, a person with a regular haunt nearby
rarer: a shrinking town, long working hours, a person who seldom goes out
tone: joy
life: friends, community
horizon: months
roles: friend, keeper, regular
earth: a café opens on the corner, with long tables and a board of what is on this week, and the old place down the road feels quieter
scene: A café has opened on the corner, with long tables and a board by the door listing what is on this week. Half of {Ns} old crowd has already been, and the old place down the road feels quieter.
scene W: {N} has gone to the same place on the same night for years. The old keeper notices who stops coming.
scene U: The board lists a talk on Tuesdays and a quiz on Thursdays. {N} wants to know who will turn up to argue.
scene B: Whoever is first through a new door gets to know the owner. {N} sees a room still deciding whose it is.
scene R: New music, new faces, and a place nobody has made rules for yet. {N} wants to be there on the opening night.
scene G: The old bar has {Ns} name on a mug behind the counter. A new place is a new place, and {N} is in no hurry.
- W | offer to set out the long tables on the new place's open community night | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: gather.W | chance: 72
- U | go to the Tuesday talk and argue the question with strangers | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: made a friend | sphere: gather.U | chance: 72
- B | get to know the owner in the first week, before anyone else does | v: power, achievement | sphere: gather.B | chance: 77
- R | be there on the opening night and stay until they stack the chairs | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 85
- G | keep to the old bar, where your name is on a mug behind the counter | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: gather.G | chance: 74
- BG | split the week between both places, and stay on good terms with both keepers | v: security, benevolence | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 66
- BR | ask the owner for the back room on Fridays, and fill it with your own crowd | v: self-direction, achievement | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: gather.BR | chance: 44
- UR | take the old quiz team to the new place, and win on the first night | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 50
- WG | ask the new owner to welcome the old regulars with a shared supper | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: gather.GW | chance: 50
- WU | help run the Tuesday talks, so that anyone who comes may speak | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: gather.WU | chance: 70
works: The new place and the old both find their crowd, and {N} has a seat in each.
works: A year on, the café on the corner feels as if it was always there, and {N} is part of why.
fails: The new place is the fashion for one summer, then half empty, and the old one has closed meanwhile.
fails: {N} drifts between the two and ends the year a regular at neither.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- keeper_dies (pairs D6a)

# world: sphere event keeper_dies, selector members, share .6
== the wake in the old bar
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: keeper_dies
share: .6
haunt: gather.house
ladder: regular
who: keeper
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: keeper_dies (sphere gather). Selector members: the regulars of a bar or hall whose ageing keeper dies with no successor ready; about 6 in 10 of the regulars feel it as more than news (share .6, estimate), once or twice in a life of going out (estimate)
likelier: years as a regular at one place, a keeper who ran it alone for decades, a small town
rarer: a chain bar with managers who come and go, a person who moves between many places
tone: mixed
life: friends, community, loss
horizon: months
roles: friend, parent, keeper, regular
earth: the owner of the bar you have gone to for years has died, and the regulars hold the wake in the bar itself
scene: The bar's owner of thirty years has died. The regulars hold the wake in the bar itself, under the photos on the wall, and someone says the place will be sold by the spring.
scene W: The owner kept a slate for those short of money and a stool for whoever came alone. {N} wonders who will keep them now.
scene U: {N} knows the place better than most: the books, the suppliers, the rent. It could be kept going, with the right plan.
scene B: A bar with a name and a crowd is worth something. {N} has heard the owner's daughter does not want it.
scene R: The owner would have hated a quiet wake. {N} means to give them the loudest night the bar has seen.
scene G: {N} first came here with {parent}. The owner knew every face in the room, and now nobody does.
- W | organise a whip-round for the owner's family and the staff out of work | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: gather.W | chance: 81
- U | draw up a plan to keep the bar open, and take it to the family | v: self-direction, achievement | sphere: gather.U | chance: 57
- B | ask the family for first refusal on the lease, before anyone else asks | v: power, achievement | lever: lead | pushes: place | sphere: gather.B | chance: 64
- R | lead the wake the way the owner would have wanted, loud and long | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: gather.R | chance: 72
- G | speak at the funeral about the owner and the old days at the bar | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: gather.G | chance: 56
- BG | keep coming whoever buys it, and tell the new owner who the old regulars are | v: security, benevolence | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 68
- UG | gather the regulars' stories and photos of the bar before they are lost | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: gather.GU | chance: 64
- UR | hold a night of stories about the owner, with the owner's favourite band after | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 66
- WB | pay for the wake, and ask the regulars to join a fund to buy the bar | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | pushes: place | sphere: gather.WB | chance: 48
- WR | rally the regulars to object together when a developer bids for the building | v: security, tradition | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: gather.RW | chance: 34
works: The bar stays open under someone who knew the old owner, and the stool by the window is still kept.
works: {N} grieves among people who understand, and comes out of that winter with friends closer than before.
fails: The bar is sold, the photos come down, and the new place has nobody's name in it.
fails: The wake is the last night the regulars spend together, and after it they scatter to other bars.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- brawl (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event brawl, selector place, share .1
== the morning after the fight outside the club
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: brawl
share: .1
haunt: gather.night
stages: young_adult adult
age: 18-50
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 3-12
times: World event: brawl (sphere gather). Selector place: a fight at closing time that puts someone in hospital, likelier with heavy drinking, crowds and young people out of work; about 1 in 10 of the young people who go out in that town know someone hurt or saw it (share .1, estimate), once or twice in the years of going out, many never (estimate)
likelier: nights out in the town centre, a crowd that drinks hard, an old feud between two sets of friends
rarer: a quiet town, a crowd that goes home early, older age
tone: trouble
life: friends, conflict, law
horizon: week
roles: friend, parent, rival
earth: outside the club at closing time a shove becomes a fight, and your friend goes to hospital
scene: Outside the club at closing time, a shove became a fight, and {friend} went to hospital with a broken cheekbone. The next morning the police want witnesses, and the other side's friends are saying {friend} started it.
scene W: {N} saw who threw the first punch. The police have asked for statements, and that is what statements are for.
scene U: The stories going round do not match. {N} wants to know what the door cameras show before saying anything.
scene B: The man who did it has a cousin who runs the door at half the clubs in town. Anything {N} says will be remembered.
scene R: {N} is still shaking with anger. Someone put {friend} in hospital, and everybody knows who.
scene G: {Ns} friend's mother has been at the hospital all night. {N} thinks first of the family.
- W | give the police a statement of exactly what you saw | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: gather.W | chance: 81
- U | ask the club for the camera footage before anyone tells their story | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 57
- B | keep your name out of it, and stay friendly with the doormen | v: security, power | sphere: gather.B | chance: 72
- R | go to his usual bar and tell him to his face what you think of him | v: stimulation, power | mark: made an enemy | sphere: gather.R | chance: 47
- G | sit with your friend's family at the hospital through the long day | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: gather.G | chance: 70
- RG | bring the old crowd to the bedside with food and music, so your friend laughs again | v: benevolence, hedonism | sphere: gather.RG | chance: 72
- UB | find out quietly who saw what, and whom the police will believe | v: power, security | sphere: gather.UB | chance: 52
- UR | write the whole night down while you are still angry, then decide what to do | v: self-direction | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 80
- WB | pay for a lawyer for your friend, and ask the regulars to chip in | v: benevolence, security | sphere: gather.WB | chance: 50
- WG | ask the elders of both families to sit down before it turns into a feud | v: security, tradition | sphere: gather.GW | chance: 34
works: The footage backs up what {N} says, and {friend} is home within the week.
works: It does not grow into a feud, and by summer the two crowds can share a street again.
fails: The stories harden into sides, and {N} cannot walk past that club again without a look over the shoulder.
fails: {friend} heals slowly, and blames {N} a little for what was or was not done.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- curfew (pairs D4b)

# world: sphere event curfew, selector place, share .5
== the bars must close at ten
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: curfew
share: .5
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 15-70
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 5-25
times: World event: curfew (sphere gather). Selector place: a rule that fears crowds sets an early closing hour in a season of unrest, war or panic; about half of the people who go out in the evenings feel it as a change in their own week (share .5, estimate), rarely more than once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: unrest in the streets, a war, a moral panic, a person who goes out most weeks
rarer: calm years, a person whose evenings are spent at home
tone: trouble
life: friends, community, law
horizon: months
roles: friend, partner, keeper
earth: a new rule says bars must close at ten, and the parties move into flats and basements
scene: A new rule says every bar must close at ten. By half past, the streets are quiet and the patrols are out, and the parties have moved into flats and basements where nobody checks the door.
scene W: A rule is a rule, and the patrols are out. {N} worries most about the people who now walk home alone at ten.
scene U: {N} wants to know who decided this, and on what figures. Nobody has said what the closing hour is meant to stop.
scene B: When the doors close at ten, someone will run the door that stays open. {N} can see who will make money from it.
scene R: Ten o'clock. The night has barely started, and {N} is not going to be sent home like a child.
scene G: The family's Saturday at the bar has become Saturday at home. {N} thinks it might not be the worst thing.
- W | keep the closing hour, and see the older regulars safely home by ten | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 77
- U | ask the council in writing what the closing hour is for, and share the answer | v: self-direction, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: gather.U | chance: 56
- B | rent a basement and run the after-hours door yourself | v: power, achievement | mark: broke the law | lever: subvert | sphere: gather.B | chance: 56
- R | go to the basement parties and walk home long after the curfew | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: defied an authority | lever: subvert | sphere: gather.R | chance: 70
- G | move the Saturday gathering to your kitchen, and invite the whole street | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 63
- BR | throw your own party in a flat, music loud, door open to friends of friends | v: hedonism, self-direction | lever: subvert | sphere: gather.BR | chance: 68
- UB | find out which bars the patrols leave alone, and why | v: power, security | sphere: gather.UB | chance: 68
- UG | start a reading evening at home on the nights the bars are shut | v: self-direction, tradition | sphere: gather.GU | chance: 68
- WG | set up a rota so nobody on the street walks home alone at night | v: benevolence, security | sphere: gather.GW | chance: 54
- WR | march against the closing hour, singing with the bar crowd | v: self-direction, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: gather.RW | chance: 40
works: The closing hour is lifted by autumn, and {N} comes through it with friends who stood together.
works: {N} finds a way to keep the evenings that matter, inside the rule or around it.
fails: The patrols stop {N} on the way home, and there is a fine and a name on a list.
fails: The bar {N} loved does not reopen, and the old crowd never gathers in one place again.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- drink_banned (pairs D5b)

# world: sphere event drink_banned, selector all, share .4
== the dry years
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: drink_banned
share: .4
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 15-40
times: World event: drink_banned (sphere gather). Selector all: a temperance or revival movement wins the rule and drink is banned across the country (the world's 'state: alcohol banned' maps onto it, spheres-implementation section 5); about 4 in 10 adults feel it as a turn in their own evenings (share .4, estimate), seldom more than once in a life (estimate)
likelier: a revival in the land, a person who goes out to drink, a town with many bars
rarer: a person who never drank, a life spent mostly at home
tone: trouble
life: friends, community, law
horizon: years
roles: friend, keeper, colleague
earth: drink is banned, the clubs serve it in teacups, and the bribes go up every month
scene: Drink is now against the law. The clubs serve it in teacups behind a knock on the door, the bribes go up every month, and the hall down the road has opened a sober reading room.
scene W: The new law says drink ruins families. {N} has seen that it can, and also that the bar was where the lonely went.
scene U: {N} reads the figures both sides wave about. They cannot all be true.
scene B: A ban makes a market. {N} knows who is already moving crates at night.
scene R: The bar was where {N} laughed, sang and forgot the week. Now it is a back room with a password.
scene G: Every family toast at every wedding is now against the law. {N} cannot see the old ones giving that up.
- W | keep the law, and help out at the sober reading room's evenings | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 75
- U | weigh what each side claims, and argue it out at the debating club | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 70
- B | sell the bottles in your cellar to the back-room clubs, at a good price | v: power, achievement | mark: broke the law | lever: subvert | sphere: gather.B | chance: 68
- R | learn the knock, and keep your Friday nights at the teacup club | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: broke the law | lever: subvert | sphere: gather.R | chance: 65
- G | brew a little at home for the family feasts, as the old ones did | v: tradition, security | mark: broke the law | sphere: gather.G | chance: 54
- BR | open a teacup club of your own at the back of a café | v: power, hedonism | mark: broke the law | lever: found | sphere: gather.BR | chance: 46
- RG | keep the dances going in the hall, with fruit punch and the same band | v: hedonism, tradition | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: gather.RG | chance: 64
- UG | learn the old soft drinks your grandmother made, and share the recipes | v: tradition, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: gather.GU | chance: 68
- WB | pay the old bar's rent through the ban, so it can open again one day | v: benevolence, tradition | lever: fund | pushes: place | sphere: gather.WB | chance: 58
- WU | put the case for repeal to the town meeting, with the facts and a vote | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: gather.WU | chance: 32
works: {N} gets through the dry years with a clean record and the friends that matter.
works: When the ban is lifted, {N} is there on the first night, and the old crowd is still a crowd.
fails: A raid on a back room puts {Ns} name in the local news.
fails: The dry years scatter the old crowd, and {N} spends many evenings alone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hall_lost (pairs D3b)

# world: sphere event hall_lost, selector members, share .6
== the flood in the community centre
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: hall_lost
share: .6
haunt: gather.hall
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: hall_lost (sphere gather). Selector members: the groups that met in a hall lost to fire, flood or storm; about 6 in 10 of their members feel the loss as their own (share .6, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it at all (estimate)
likelier: an old building, a flood plain, years in one of the hall's groups
rarer: a new building, a person in no club or group
tone: mixed
life: community, friends, home
horizon: years
roles: friend, grandparent, elder, patron, regular
earth: a flood ruins the community centre, and for a year its groups meet in kitchens or not at all
scene: The flood has ruined the community centre: the floor is up, the chairs are gone, and the noticeboard is pulp. For a year its groups will meet in kitchens, or not at all.
scene W: Every Tuesday for years the hall was open for anyone. {N} thinks of the people who had nowhere else to go.
scene U: {N} wants to know whether the building can be saved, what it would cost, and who would pay.
scene B: A rich family in {place} has offered to pay for the new roof. {N} wonders what they will want in return.
scene R: The mud is still on the walls, and {N} is already itching to get in there with a shovel and some music.
scene G: {N} danced at a wedding in that hall, and stood at the wake for {grandparent}. The building holds half a life.
- W | turn up with gloves every Saturday until the hall is cleared | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: gather.W | chance: 72
- U | get the building surveyed, and work out what saving it truly costs | v: self-direction, security | sphere: gather.U | chance: 72
- B | take the rich family's money, and get your group the best room in the new hall | v: power, achievement | sphere: gather.B | chance: 75
- R | throw a fundraising party in the car park, mud and all | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: gather.R | chance: 75
- G | host your group in your own kitchen every week until the hall is back | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 67
- BR | start a new night of your own in a rented room while the hall is shut | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | sphere: gather.BR | chance: 56
- UG | save the old photos and records from the mud, and dry them page by page | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: gather.GU | chance: 62
- UR | draw up a better hall with the young members, and show it at the meeting | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 52
- WB | join the committee that spends the rebuilding money, and share it among every group | v: power, universalism | lever: lead | pushes: place | sphere: gather.WB | chance: 52
- WG | hold a shared supper each month so the scattered groups still meet | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: gather.GW | chance: 62
works: The hall reopens the next autumn, and {N} is in the room when the first group meets again.
works: The year of kitchens brings the neighbours closer than the hall ever did.
fails: The money never comes, and the hall stays boarded up with the old noticeboard still on the wall.
fails: Two of the groups never meet again, and {N} misses them more than expected.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- peace_feast (pairs D3a)

# world: sphere event peace_feast, selector place, share .6
== long tables in the street when the war ends
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: peace_feast
share: .6
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-60
times: World event: peace_feast (sphere gather). Selector place: the first great gathering after a war, a siege, an epidemic or a long ban ends; about 6 in 10 of the people living there remember it as a night of their own (share .6, estimate), once in a life for most who live through a war (estimate)
likelier: a long war or ban just over, a soldier home in the family, a town that lost many
rarer: a place far from the war, a family in mourning
tone: joy
life: community, family, love
horizon: week
roles: friend, sibling, prospect, partner
earth: the war is over and the soldiers are home: the street puts out long tables, and the bars stay open until dawn
scene: The war is over and the soldiers are home. The street has put out long tables, every bar is open until dawn, and people who have not laughed in years are dancing in the road.
scene W: {N} thinks of the families whose soldier is not coming home. Someone should make sure they are not left at the edge of the party.
scene U: {N} keeps listening to the soldiers' stories. Nobody tells the war the way the news did.
scene B: Everyone in {place} is out tonight, and everyone is in a giving mood. {N} notices who is talking to whom.
scene R: Years of fear, gone in one night. {N} wants to dance until the sun comes up.
scene G: {sibling} is home. That is all {N} can think about: the whole family at one table again.
- W | fetch the families who lost someone, and give them the first seats at the table | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: gather.W | chance: 76
- U | sit with the soldiers and listen to what the war was really like | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: gather.U | chance: 84
- B | spend the night meeting everyone who matters, while every door is open | v: power, achievement | mark: made a friend | sphere: gather.B | chance: 83
- R | dance in the street with strangers until dawn | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 85
- G | carry the family table out into the street and cook the dish everyone missed | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: gather.G | chance: 85
- BG | sit with the soldier nobody wants to talk to, and keep the drinks coming | v: benevolence | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 72
- RG | ask the one you have been watching all night to dance | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: made a friend | sphere: gather.RG | chance: 52
- UB | introduce the soldiers home without work to the people who are hiring | v: achievement, benevolence | sphere: gather.UB | chance: 56
- WR | lead the whole street in the old songs from before the war | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: gather.RW | chance: 72
- WU | set up a table where people can ask after the missing and the found | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: gather.WU | chance: 70
works: {N} remembers that night for the rest of {Ns} life, and so does someone {N} met there.
works: The street keeps one long table every year after, on the same night.
fails: Past midnight the grief catches up, and {N} ends the night in tears on a doorstep.
fails: Too much drink and too many feelings, and {N} says something to {sibling} that is hard to take back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- slump_shifts (pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event slump_shifts, selector place, share .4
== hard times fill the soup night
tier: life event
sphere: gather
sphere_event: slump_shifts
share: .4
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 6-20
times: World event: slump_shifts (sphere gather). Selector place: a slump or lean year of a year or more moves the town's evenings to cheap and free places; about 4 in 10 of the people living there feel their own evenings change (share .4, estimate), two or three times in a life (estimate)
likelier: a slump, work lost in the family, a town with one big employer
rarer: a person in secure work, a town the slump passes by
