scene: The old rail yard has become a park, with a skate bowl, a market square and long benches. On summer nights half of {place} is there, and {N} keeps meeting people from streets {N} has never walked down.
scene W: A place that belongs to everyone needs looking after by everyone. {N} has noticed the bins are already full.
scene U: The benches by the market are where the old men argue about everything. {N} has started to join in.
scene B: The market square has stalls to let. {N} sees a chance.
scene R: The skate bowl, the music on the benches, the warm nights. {N} is there every evening.
scene G: Sunday picnics on the grass, three families pushed together. It feels like the old village feast, {grandparent} says.
